post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> Kahawai runs as the "kahawai" user and reads /etc/kahawai/kahawai.toml.
    Add collections there and give that user read access to them, then:
      systemctl enable --now kahawai.service    # all-in-one
    or run roles separately: kahawai-hub, kahawai-mediahost and
    kahawai-transcoder.service (see the end of the config).
==> Create the first administrator once the hub runs: open
    http://127.0.0.1:8422 on this machine, or
      sudo -u kahawai kahawai --config /etc/kahawai/kahawai.toml hub init-admin
MSG
}
